  26:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  27:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   ==============================================================================
  28:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  29:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     This driver implements a high level communication layer for read and write from/to
  30:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     this memory. The needed STM32 hardware resources (SDMMC and GPIO) are performed by
  31:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     the user in HAL_SD_MspInit() function (MSP layer).
  32:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     Basically, the MSP layer configuration should be the same as we provide in the
  33:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     examples.
  34:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     You can easily tailor this configuration according to hardware resources.
  35:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  36:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  37:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     This driver is a generic layered driver for SDMMC memories which uses the HAL
  38:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     SDMMC driver functions to interface with SD and uSD cards devices.
  39:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     It is used as follows:
  40:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  41:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#)Initialize the SDMMC low level resources by implementing the HAL_SD_MspInit() API:
  42:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) Enable the SDMMC interface clock using __HAL_RCC_SDMMC_CLK_ENABLE();
  43:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) SDMMC pins configuration for SD card
  44:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the clock for the SDMMC GPIOs using the functions __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENAB
  45:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure these SDMMC pins as alternate function pull-up using HAL_GPIO_Init()
  46:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and according to your pin assignment;
  47:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process (HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_IT()
  48:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****              and HAL_SD_WriteBlocks_IT() APIs).
  49:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Configure the SDMMC interrupt priorities using function HAL_NVIC_SetPriority();
  50:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC SDMMC IRQs using function HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  51:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDMMC interrupts are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_ENABLE_IT()
  52:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_DISABLE_IT() inside the communication process.
  53:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****             (+++) SDMMC interrupts pending bits are managed using the macros __HAL_SD_GET_IT()
  54:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****                   and __HAL_SD_CLEAR_IT()
  55:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         (##) No general propose DMA Configuration is needed, an Internal DMA for SDMMC Peripheral a
  56:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  57:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) At this stage, you can perform SD read/write/erase operations after SD card initialization
  58:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  59:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** SD Card Initialization and configuration ***
  60:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   ================================================
  61:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  62:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     To initialize the SD Card, use the HAL_SD_Init() function. It Initializes
  63:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     SDMMC Peripheral(STM32 side) and the SD Card, and put it into StandBy State (Ready for data tra
  64:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function provide the following operations:
  65:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  66:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Apply the SD Card initialization process at 400KHz and check the SD Card
  67:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         type (Standard Capacity or High Capacity). You can change or adapt this
  68:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         frequency by adjusting the "ClockDiv" field.
  69:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         The SD Card frequency (SDMMC_CK) is computed as follows:
  70:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  71:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****            SDMMC_CK = SDMMCCLK / (2 * ClockDiv)
  72:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  73:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         In initialization mode and according to the SD Card standard,
  74:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         make sure that the SDMMC_CK frequency doesn't exceed 400KHz.
  75:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  76:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         This phase of initialization is done through SDMMC_Init() and
  77:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         SDMMC_PowerState_ON() SDMMC low level APIs.
  78:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  79:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Initialize the SD card. The API used is HAL_SD_InitCard().
  80:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         This phase allows the card initialization and identification
  81:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         and check the SD Card type (Standard Capacity or High Capacity)
  82:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         The initialization flow is compatible with SD standard.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Antonio\AppData\Local\Temp\ccd2j2xW.s 			page 3


  83:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  84:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         This API (HAL_SD_InitCard()) could be used also to reinitialize the card in case
  85:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         of plug-off plug-in.
  86:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  87:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Configure the SD Card Data transfer frequency. You can change or adapt this
  88:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         frequency by adjusting the "ClockDiv" field.
  89:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         In transfer mode and according to the SD Card standard, make sure that the
  90:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         SDMMC_CK frequency doesn't exceed 25MHz and 100MHz in High-speed mode switch.
  91:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  92:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Select the corresponding SD Card according to the address read with the step 2.
  93:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  94:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (#) Configure the SD Card in wide bus mode: 4-bits data.
  95:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
  96:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** SD Card Read operation ***
  97:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   ==============================
  98:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
  99:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in polling mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks().
 100:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 101:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 102:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 103:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 104:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 105:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 106:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 107:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in DMA mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_DMA().
 108:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 109:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 110:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 111:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 112:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 113:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 114:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         You could also check the DMA transfer process through the SD Rx interrupt event.
 115:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 116:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can read from SD card in Interrupt mode by using function HAL_SD_ReadBlocks_IT().
 117:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 118:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 119:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 120:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 121:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 122:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 123:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         You could also check the IT transfer process through the SD Rx interrupt event.
 124:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 125:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   *** SD Card Write operation ***
 126:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   ===============================
 127:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   [..]
 128:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can write to SD card in polling mode by using function HAL_SD_WriteBlocks().
 129:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 130:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
 131:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         You can choose either one block read operation or multiple block read operation
 132:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         by adjusting the "NumberOfBlocks" parameter.
 133:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         After this, you have to ensure that the transfer is done correctly. The check is done
 134:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         through HAL_SD_GetCardState() function for SD card state.
 135:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 136:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     (+) You can write to SD card in DMA mode by using function HAL_SD_WriteBlocks_DMA().
 137:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         This function support only 512-bytes block length (the block size should be
 138:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****         chosen as 512 bytes).
