 202:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Read_DMADblBuf1CpltCallback : callback when the DMA reception of second buffer is complet
 203:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Write_DMADblBuf0CpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of first buffer is comp
 204:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Write_DMADblBuf1CpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of second buffer is com
 205:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SD MspInit.
 206:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SD MspDeInit.
 207:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 208:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     and a pointer to the user callback function.
 209:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     For specific callbacks TransceiverCallback use dedicated register callbacks:
 210:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     respectively HAL_SD_RegisterTransceiverCallback().
 211:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 212:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     Use function HAL_SD_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 213:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     weak (overridden) function. It allows to reset following callbacks:
 214:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback : callback when a transmission transfer is completed.
 215:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback : callback when a reception transfer is completed.
 216:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback : callback when error occurs.
 217:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) AbortCpltCallback : callback when abort is completed.
 218:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Read_DMALnkLstBufCpltCallback : callback when the DMA reception of linked list node buffe
 219:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) Write_DMALnkLstBufCpltCallback : callback when the DMA transmission of linked list node b
 220:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SD MspInit.
 221:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SD MspDeInit.
 222:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     This function) takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle and the Callback ID.
 223:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     For specific callbacks TransceiverCallback use dedicated unregister callbacks:
 224:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     respectively HAL_SD_UnRegisterTransceiverCallback().
 225:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 226:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     By default, after the HAL_SD_Init and if the state is HAL_SD_STATE_RESET
 227:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     all callbacks are reset to the corresponding legacy weak (overridden) functions.
 228:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit callbacks that are respectively
 229:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     reset to the legacy weak (overridden) functions in the HAL_SD_Init
 230:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     and HAL_SD_DeInit only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 231:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_SD_Init and HAL_SD_DeInit
 232:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand)
 233:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 234:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in READY state only.
 235:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     Exception done for MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks that can be registered/unregistered
 236:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     in READY or RESET state, thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used
 237:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     during the Init/DeInit.
 238:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 239:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     using HAL_SD_RegisterCallback before calling HAL_SD_DeInit
 240:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     or HAL_SD_Init function.
 241:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 242:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     When The compilation define USE_HAL_SD_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 243:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     not defined, the callback registering feature is not available
 244:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****     and weak (overridden) callbacks are used.
 245:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c **** 
 246:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   @endverbatim
 247:../../STM32Cube_FW_N6/Drivers/STM32N6xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32n6xx_hal_sd.c ****   ******************************************************************************
